Package: evca
Title: Expected Value of Causal Ambiguity
Version: 0.5.0
Description: Provides decision-analytic diagnostics for structural
    uncertainty and contested causal models. The package computes the
    shortfall between a weighted aggregate decision and a disaggregation
    benchmark, plus leave-one-model-out exclusion costs. With epistemic model
    probabilities, the shortfall has the expected value of perfect information
    interpretation for a model index. With evaluative model weights, it is an
    aggregation diagnostic conditional on the chosen weights and common-scale
    bridge, not a value of research. The package operates on pre-computed
    expected utilities; model construction, utility elicitation, and defensible
    cross-model scaling remain the analyst's responsibility.
